% Annex A: Summary of ER Methodologies
% ============================================================
\section{Summary of Entity Resolution Methodologies}
\label{annex:er_methodologies}

This annex provides a structured overview of major ER approaches, their inference styles, and the problem structures they address.
The choice of method is dictated by the constraints of the specific ER problem (data types, label availability, scale, attribute semantics).

\begin{longtable}{p{2.5cm}p{2.5cm}p{3.5cm}p{3.5cm}p{3.5cm}}
\toprule
\textbf{Method Family} & \textbf{Inference Style} & \textbf{Problem Structure} & \textbf{Key Assumptions} & \textbf{Limitations} \\
\midrule
\endhead

\fellegisunter{} (FS) & EM / MLE (unsupervised) & Pairwise classification; record pairs independent given match status & Conditional independence of fields; stationarity; comparison functions fixed & Independence violated in practice; requires good comparison functions; no transitive consistency \\

Bayesian Networks / Graphical Models & MCMC / Variational Inference & Collective resolution; dependencies between pairs & Graph structure captures dependencies; prior knowledge encodable & Computationally heavy; requires structure learning or domain specification \\

Hierarchical Clustering & Agglomerative / Divisive & No labels; distance matrix given & Metric space; linkage criterion matches cluster shape & $\mathcal{O}(n^2)$ or $\mathcal{O}(n^3)$; sensitive to noise; no probabilistic output \\

Correlation Clustering & ILP / LP Relaxation / Approx & Partition into clusters; pairwise similarity & Objective: maximise agreements minus disagreements & NP-hard; approximations lose guarantees; no explicit match probabilities \\

Supervised Binary Classification & Gradient Boosting / NN / SVM & Labelled pairs; features from record pairs & IID pairs; sufficient labels; feature engineering captures signal & Needs labels; pairs not IID (transitivity); class imbalance severe \\

Learning to Rank & LambdaMART / ListNet & Rank candidates for each query record & Relevance grades available; listwise objective & Needs labelled lists; pointwise reduction loses list structure \\

Deep Metric Learning / Siamese Nets & Contrastive / Triplet Loss & Learn embedding where matches are close & Large labelled data; architecture captures semantics & Black box; needs massive data; no direct probability \\

LLM Semantic Matching & Prompting / Fine-tuning / Embeddings & Text-heavy records; semantic equivalence & LLM understands domain; prompts generalise & Costly; non-deterministic; hard to calibrate; no structure exploited \\

Graph / Behavioural ER & Message Passing / GNN / Random Walk & Network / transactional data; behaviour defines identity & Entity behaviour is distinctive; graph structure informative & Requires graph construction; different feature space (behavioural vs attribute) \\

Canonicalisation / Standardisation + Exact Match & Rule-based / Deterministic & Cleanable attributes; canonical forms exist & Rules are complete and correct & Brittle; manual effort; fails on fuzzy/noisy data \\

Local-to-Global (This Work) & FS + Aggregation (unsupervised) & Stable within-dataset IDs; multi-record entities & Within-dataset ID stability; attribute types (text/num/date); conditional independence & Fails at low cardinality (indep breaks); 2 datasets only; static entities \\

\bottomrule
\end{longtable}

\textbf{Decision Guidance}:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textit{No labels, attribute data, stable IDs $\to$ FS (this work)}
    \item \textit{No labels, attribute data, NO stable IDs $\to$ Clustering / Graphical Models}
    \item \textit{Labels available, attribute data $\to$ Supervised / LTR / Deep Metric}
    \item \textit{Text-heavy, semantic variation $\to$ LLM Embeddings + FS/Supervised}
    \item \textit{Behavioural / Network data $\to$ Graph ER / GNN}
    \item \textit{Multi-source ($>2$), transitive consistency needed $\to$ Collective / Graphical}
    \item \textit{Temporal evolution $\to$ State-space / Incremental}
\end{itemize}